.TH SDL_Locale 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_Locale \- A struct to provide locale data.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_locale.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_Locale
.BI "{
.BI "    const char *language;  /**< A language name, like \(dqen\(dq for English. */
.BI "    const char *country;  /**< A country, like \(dqUS\(dq for America. Can be NULL. */
.BI "} SDL_Locale;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Locale data is split into a spoken language, like English, and an optional country, like Canada\[char46]
.PP
Language strings are ISO-639 language specifiers (such as \(dqen\(dq for English, \(dqde\(dq for German, etc)\[char46] Country strings are ISO-3166 country codes (such as \(dqUS\(dq for the United States, \(dqCA\(dq for Canada, etc)\[char46] The country might be NULL if there\(aqs no specific guidance on them (so you might have
.BR "{ \(dqen\(dq, \(dqUS\(dq }"
for American English, but
.BR "{ \(dqen\(dq, NULL }"
means \(dqEnglish language, generically\(dq)\[char46] Language strings are never NULL\[char46]
.PP
Please note that not all of these strings are 2 characters; some are three or more\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetPreferredLocales (3)
